---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Considered documentation"
  description="Repository policy and decision documentation for codebases."
  current="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Enforce standards, document exceptions</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Considered evaluates repository metrics against declared standards and
      records intentional exceptions with their reasons. Keep the policy and
      the decisions behind it in your repository, and enforce them locally and
      in CI.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="quick-start/">Quick start</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="configuration/">Configuration guide</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it records</h2>
    <div class="grid" aria-label="Core concepts">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Standards</h3>
        <p>
          Repository-wide metric boundaries such as code lines, complexity,
          file bytes, and longest line.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Violations</h3>
        <p>
          Values outside the configured standard. Violations fail checks and
          deserve attention.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Variances</h3>
        <p>
          Reviewed departures from standards, tied to exact files and recorded
          with a reason.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc">
    <h2>How evaluation works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Collect a metric value from its provider.</li>
      <li>Apply the matching standard.</li>
      <li>
        If the value is within the standard, it passes. Near-boundary values can
        also be reported as non-failing warnings.
      </li>
      <li>
        If the value falls outside the standard, Considered checks for a variance on
        the exact subject and metric.
      </li>
      <li>
        A value inside the variance boundary passes as a visible variance. A
        missing or out-of-range variance is a violation.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
